          "notes": [
            {
              "no": 1,
              "type": "VOUCHER",
              "note": "Lounge Directions.\nThe No1 Lounge is located Airside at Terminal 3.  Once through security follow the walkway to the left of World Duty Free and then follow signs for Airline Lounge F. \nNo.1 Lounge Heathrow is one floor up.\n\nDress Code:\nThe lounge has a smart casual dress code (no baseball caps, shorts or sports shirts,beach flip flops, vests, themed or fancy-dress outfits, clothes with slogans that may cause offense, clothing that may expose midriffs or upper thighs) and expects reasonable behaviour from all guests.\nLarge groups and families with young children are asked to respect other No1 customers and keep noise levels down.\nHen/stag parties are not permitted.\nAnyone who refuses to adhere to these requirements will be refused access and forfeit the right to any refund.\n\nWe have a responsibility to ensure guests are fit to fly. If you appear intoxicated, you\u0027ll be refused entry to your flight.\n\n\nMaximum stay 3 hours prior to flight departure.",
              "systemGenerated": true,
              "noteId": 0
            },
            {
              "no": 2,
              "type": "INVOICE",
              "note": "Lounge Information:\nLocated Airside. After customs.\nChildren welcome.\nMaximum stay 3 hours prior to flight departure.  Extra hours can be purchased in advance if you plan to arrive earlier.\n\nDress Code:\nThe lounge has a smart casual dress code (no baseball caps, shorts or football shirts) and expects reasonable behaviour from all guests.\nLarge groups and families with young children are asked to respect other No1 customers and keep noise levels down.\nHen/stag parties are not permitted.",
              "systemGenerated": true,
              "noteId": 0
            },
            {
              "no": 3,
              "type": "ITINERARY",
              "note": "Lounge Information:\nLocated Airside. After customs.\nChildren welcome.\nMaximum stay 3 hours prior to flight departure.  Extra hours can be purchased in advance if you plan to arrive earlier.\n\nDress Code:\nThe lounge has a smart casual dress code (no baseball caps, shorts or football shirts) and expects reasonable behaviour from all guests.\nLarge groups and families with young children are asked to respect other No1 customers and keep noise levels down.\nHen/stag parties are not permitted.",
              "systemGenerated": true,
              "noteId": 0
            },
            {
              "no": 4,
              "type": "INVOICE",
              "note": "Food and Drinks:\n\nBreakfast is available from 4am - 11am.\nComplimentary buffet comprising of freshly baked pastries, fruit salad, yoghurt, cereals, toast.\nComplimentary hot dishes from the kitchen: No.1 Poached Pot (poached egg pot served with granary bread), warm bacon roll, warm omelette roll.\n\nThe day menu is available from 11am - 10pm.\nComplimentary buffet including antipasti, cheese, salads, tartlets, cakes, brownies and fresh fruit.\nComplimentary hot dishes from the kitchen: Soup of the day, No.1 Poached Pot and classic welsh rarebit.\n\nAll dishes change seasonally.  Gluten free and dairy free dishes available.\n\nThe bar is open from lounge opening time to lounge closing time.\nComplimentary drinks (including alcohol). Only well-known premium brands are served.\nTea and coffee stations thoughout the lounge.\nFridges with soft drinks, including sodas and water, throughout the lounge.\n\nLounge Facilities:\nTV, newspapers, magazines, free WI-FI, computers, plugs, faxing, scanning\nCinema\nQuiet \u0027snug\u0027 room\nLibrary\nToilets \u0026 showers\nFlight information screens\nRunway views\nFriendly uniformed staff.  Credit card is accepted.\n",
              "systemGenerated": true,
              "noteId": 0
            },
            {
              "no": 5,
              "type": "ITINERARY",
              "note": "Food and Drinks:\n\nBreakfast is available from 4am - 11am.\nComplimentary buffet comprising of freshly baked pastries, fruit salad, yoghurt, cereals, toast.\nComplimentary hot dishes from the kitchen: No.1 Poached Pot (poached egg pot served with granary bread), warm bacon roll, warm omelette roll.\n\nThe day menu is available from 11am - 10pm.\nComplimentary buffet including antipasti, cheese, salads, tartlets, cakes, brownies and fresh fruit.\nComplimentary hot dishes from the kitchen: Soup of the day, No.1 Poached Pot and classic welsh rarebit.\n\nAll dishes change seasonally.  Gluten free and dairy free dishes available.\n\nThe bar is open from lounge opening time to lounge closing time.\nComplimentary drinks (including alcohol). Only well-known premium brands are served.\nTea and coffee stations thoughout the lounge.\nFridges with soft drinks, including sodas and water, throughout the lounge.\n\nLounge Facilities:\nTV, newspapers, magazines, free WI-FI, computers, plugs, faxing, scanning\nCinema\nQuiet \u0027snug\u0027 room\nLibrary\nToilets \u0026 showers\nFlight information screens\nRunway views\nFriendly uniformed staff.  Credit card is accepted.\n",
